---
import Section from './Section.astro';
import Terminal from './Terminal.astro';
import Tui from './Tui.astro';
---

<Section id="monitor" title="See what every lane and service costs, live." stacked>
  <p>
    Running <code>devlanes</code> opens a terminal view of every lane in the project, with the state
    of each service and its live output. The monitor shows CPU and memory per lane, per service and
    per container, with a minute of history, so you can tell which worktree is eating the memory.
    Open a unit to read its output, type into it, stop it or restart it.
  </p>
  <div slot="visual" class="tui-try">
    <p>This is the real TUI, running as a WebAssembly bundle on fake data. Click to interact.</p>
    <Terminal title="devlanes" class="terminal-tui">
      <Tui />
    </Terminal>
    <a class="more" href="/docs/getting-started/#tui">
      The TUI in the docs
    </a>
  </div>
</Section>
